# Scheduled jobs for the worker container (supercronic, runs as www-data, UTC).
# This default only has jobs that are safe on any environment.
# On the droplet, point CRONTAB at the deployment's own crontab, which also runs
# maintenance, the monthly cleanups and the status check.
#
# Each job goes through `cronjob <slug> <command>` (docker/worker/cronjob.sh):
# per-run log in /var/www/log/cron/, healthchecks.io pings when
# HEALTHCHECKSIO_PING_KEY is set.

# Daily: drop old queue tasks (45 days), old per-task/cron logs (15 days) and tmp files (3 days).
17 3 * * *  cronjob cleanup 'cd /var/www/html/prod/api/queue && php queuectl.php clean && find /var/www/log -type f -mtime +15 -delete && find /var/www/tmp -type f -mtime +3 -delete'
